WEBVTT

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:05.610
<i>Monsters threaten human life.</i>

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:09.660
<i>They are opposed by brave adventurers!</i>

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:14.530
And I, Alvin, am one of them!

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:18.490
Now in a party with Carla, the healer,

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:21.390
my journey continues!

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.350
Don't Hurt Me,

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.350
Don't Hurt Me,

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.350
My Healer!

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:58.930
<b>This show is fairly unique in that Carla is the only recurring female character...</b>

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:58.990
Another peaceful day.

00:01:58.990 --> 00:02:00.120
Yeah...

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:03.630
But peace isn't exactly 
conducive to leveling up.

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:06.520
Wonder where we could find some monsters...

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:07.540
Weak ones, you mean?

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:08.760
Shut up.

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:11.780
Is that...

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.910
Someone's collapsed over there!

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:17.960
Attacked by a monster, perhaps?

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:20.870
Never mind that, Alvin-san!

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:21.410
Hurry!

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:22.910
Right!

00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:24.490
Hurry up and bury them!

00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:25.840
Don't jump to conclusions!

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:28.580
You can't just assume a 
person like that is dead!

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:33.060
But nine times out of ten, when you see 
someone collapsed on the road, they're dead.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:34.960
We don't know that for sure!

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:36.330
Very well.

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:38.270
We just have to check first, then?

00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:39.960
Of course we do!

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:43.520
And after we check, we can bury them?

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:45.340
That depends on what we find!

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:48.670
You think we might find that 
cremation is preferable?

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:50.900
Which is better, that or burial?

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:53.020
At least consider the chance 
that he might be alive!

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:54.650
Fine, forget you.

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:56.160
I'll check him myself!

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:57.920
Shoo, shoo.

00:02:58.290 --> 00:02:59.790
Stop!

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:01.420
Hang on just a mushroom!

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:02.610
What now?

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:03.880
And have you been here this whole time?

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:06.210
It's not safe to approach so incautiously.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:11.570
Some monsters pretend to be 
human to get your guard down.

00:03:11.570 --> 00:03:14.330
There's no guarantee that's a person!

00:03:14.690 --> 00:03:15.830
Good point.

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:19.420
Gosh. Shouldn't you do a little studying 
before you become an adventurer?

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:22.370
I don't like hearing that from a monster...

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:26.460
But there's also a chance 
that they really are human...

00:03:26.690 --> 00:03:29.020
Then why not call out to them first?

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:30.780
By all means, Alvin-san, go ahead.

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:32.140
Me?!

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:33.970
Fine, but...

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:36.980
Hey! Are you alive?

00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:39.600
That seems a bit insensitive.

00:03:40.050 --> 00:03:42.360
Hey! How you doing?

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:43.860
More friendly!

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:46.120
Wanna go out for tea together?

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:49.120
Sorry. You're not my type.

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:51.320
I wasn't talking to you!

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:53.210
And why are you making me say these things?

00:03:53.930 --> 00:03:57.990
Only a cockroach of a man would 
say exactly what he's told to.

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:04.900
He's moving!

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:06.890
Thank goodness! He's alive!

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:09.360
That means we won't have to bury him!

00:04:11.130 --> 00:04:12.950
No, he really is dead!

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:14.600
We really <i>should</i> have buried him!

00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:25.990
Hang on. Can this zombie not stand up?

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:32.780
Awesome! Even I can beat this thing!

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:33.590
Don't you dare!

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:38.330
Don't his attempts to stand 
inspire any feeling in you?

00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:40.080
The feeling that I can beat him, sure!

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:43.330
Even zombies are just trying 
to live their lives!

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:45.030
But they're dead!

00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:47.740
And you're the one who wanted to bury him!

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:50.560
I was moved by his passion!

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:57.060
Don't give up!

00:04:57.060 --> 00:04:58.920
Don't let the rot take your spirit, too!

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:00.010
Give it your best!

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:05.290
Almost there!

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:10.960
One more time!

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:50.080
Come on, man! Give it all you got!

00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:03.680
H-He stood up!

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:05.640
The zombie...

00:06:05.980 --> 00:06:07.800
The zombie stood up!

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:10.670
The zombie stood up!

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:12.620
The zombie stood up!

00:06:12.620 --> 00:06:13.650
The zombie—

00:06:14.950 --> 00:06:17.710
The zombie... stood up!

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:28.060
I've never seen anything so moving!

00:06:28.060 --> 00:06:29.280
It's awesome!

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:33.930
You...

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:37.550
You have true grit.

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:40.530
What?

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:48.120
H-His head!

00:06:48.460 --> 00:06:49.460
I didn't...

00:06:49.460 --> 00:06:50.380
I didn't do it on purpose!

00:06:51.810 --> 00:06:53.720
Y-You killed him!

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:56.130
But he was already dead!

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:05.020
We did bury him, at least...

00:07:05.310 --> 00:07:08.420
But aren't zombies supposed 
to come back to life?

00:07:08.420 --> 00:07:09.780
There's no need to worry.

00:07:10.230 --> 00:07:15.130
The prayers of one with a holy 
spirit can purify his soul.

00:07:15.130 --> 00:07:16.650
So, not you, then?

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:21.230
Sorrowful being, wandering this 
world even after death...

00:07:21.230 --> 00:07:24.540
Find peaceful slumber, and 
when the dawn comes...

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:26.480
Awaken!

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:28.170
Why are you waking him up?!

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:33.190
See? You woke him up!

00:07:33.190 --> 00:07:34.440
Oh, drat!

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:36.530
I accidentally rejuvenated him.

00:07:37.090 --> 00:07:39.440
That's not rejuvenation!

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:42.750
So, this is holy power!

00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:44.460
I feel so refreshed!

00:07:44.460 --> 00:07:46.310
But you're still decapitated!

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:48.700
Thank you for waking me up!

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:50.990
I am Zobita, the zombie!

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:52.450
What a lazy name.

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:54.830
I am Carla.

00:07:54.830 --> 00:07:56.710
A bonafide healer!

00:07:56.710 --> 00:07:59.520
Bonafide? Don't make me laugh.

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:02.210
And this is Alvin-san, the laughingstock.

00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:03.280
I'm a <i>warrior</i>!

00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:05.700
And I am the beloved mascot—

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:06.720
Shut up, would you?

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:09.660
A healer, a laughingstock, and a mushroom.

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:11.840
What an unusual party!

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:14.250
He just called us unusual, Alvin-san!

00:08:14.250 --> 00:08:16.870
Isn't that a nice compliment, <i>Carla</i>?

00:08:16.870 --> 00:08:18.970
Are you adventurers?

00:08:18.970 --> 00:08:21.260
What a happy coincidence!

00:08:21.260 --> 00:08:22.850
Can I ask you for a favor?

00:08:23.110 --> 00:08:24.890
Very well. We'll do it!

00:08:24.890 --> 00:08:25.800
Not so fast!

00:08:26.070 --> 00:08:28.810
We don't take requests from monsters!

00:08:28.810 --> 00:08:30.490
But we could earn his gratitude.

00:08:30.490 --> 00:08:31.910
She's so damned obvious!

00:08:31.910 --> 00:08:34.710
I'm obviously trying to get him in my debt.

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:38.170
Do you have any motives 
that aren't ulterior ones?

00:08:38.170 --> 00:08:40.610
And you never got any better at that wink...

00:08:40.610 --> 00:08:43.450
Now, what's the favor you wanted to ask?

00:08:43.450 --> 00:08:44.990
It is...

00:08:48.660 --> 00:08:50.630
Revenge!

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:50.630
<b>Revenge</b>

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:55.300
<b>Revenge</b>

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:56.210
Let's review.

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:58.890
<b>Review</b>

00:08:56.210 --> 00:08:58.890
Great idea. Shut up and do that.

00:08:59.250 --> 00:09:02.100
Revenge is a messy business, though.

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:03.430
Care to fill us in on the story?

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:06.540
His grades must be down, 
since he didn't review enough.

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:07.770
Don't make fun!

00:09:08.120 --> 00:09:13.320
Down this road lies a graveyard so old, 
that all people have forgotten its name.

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:14.800
That is where...

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:23.860
I served as leader of the all-zombie 
dance troupe, Be Zombitious!

00:09:23.860 --> 00:09:26.240
We <i>are</i> talking about revenge, aren't we?

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:29.010
Then one day, out of the blue...

00:09:29.280 --> 00:09:32.890
a terrible necromancer arrived!

00:09:36.570 --> 00:09:38.350
It wasn't me!

00:09:38.350 --> 00:09:40.210
Remember, I'm a healer!

00:09:40.210 --> 00:09:41.810
I didn't say anything.

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:45.290
The necromancer's level was so high...

00:09:45.290 --> 00:09:49.340
And one after another, my fellow 
zombies became taken in...

00:09:49.570 --> 00:09:55.120
I have heard that high-level necromancers 
can enslave the souls of the dead...

00:09:57.560 --> 00:10:01.380
Taken in by her amazing dance skills!

00:10:01.380 --> 00:10:02.250
Oh!

00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:04.080
So cool!

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:05.950
She sounds more like a dancer!

00:10:07.650 --> 00:10:12.180
I can't let her dancing be better 
than mine, the group leader!

00:10:12.180 --> 00:10:15.170
I want revenge against 
her for humiliating me!

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:17.170
This sounds more like a petty grudge.

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:19.040
Whatever the reason,

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:21.860
we can hardly leave a necromancer at large.

00:10:21.860 --> 00:10:24.210
We will help you achieve your revenge!

00:10:24.210 --> 00:10:28.030
I know someone even worse is 
being left at large, myself.

00:10:28.030 --> 00:10:31.710
Still, I do think this job is for us.

00:10:31.710 --> 00:10:32.820
How so?

00:10:33.130 --> 00:10:36.640
Necromancers are weak against holy power.

00:10:36.640 --> 00:10:38.320
In other words, I hold the advantage!

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:40.330
You don't have holy anything.

00:10:40.330 --> 00:10:43.540
And you're a master dancer, Alvin-san!

00:10:44.530 --> 00:10:47.710
When someone's pulling your 
strings, you dance so good!

00:10:47.710 --> 00:10:48.950
Wee, wee!

00:10:48.950 --> 00:10:50.220
Wee, wee!

00:10:50.220 --> 00:10:51.960
Don't want to be good at that!

00:10:52.490 --> 00:10:53.840
Now, let's go!

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:56.560
To the unknown graveyard!

00:10:56.560 --> 00:10:58.480
Wait! You're really going?!

00:10:58.480 --> 00:11:00.960
Thanks for the help!

00:11:13.390 --> 00:11:15.520
W-Wait a minute!

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:19.900
Wait a minute! Stop!

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:23.900
Why are you running away?

00:11:27.900 --> 00:11:31.890
This fast zombie trend is 
such a problem for me.

00:11:31.890 --> 00:11:34.290
Hey, Carla. What in the world are you—

00:11:34.290 --> 00:11:36.540
What is that in your hands?

00:11:36.540 --> 00:11:39.010
I call it the flame of salvation.

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:42.420
It purges the souls of the dead with fire.

00:11:42.420 --> 00:11:44.420
It's the holy magic of Hell.

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:48.060
There is no holiness or salvation 
in anything you're saying.

00:11:48.360 --> 00:11:52.820
And have you forgotten that we came to 
this graveyard for the necromancer?

00:11:52.820 --> 00:11:54.330
It's all right.

00:11:54.330 --> 00:11:57.010
If we start enough trouble, 
she'll come to us eventually.

00:11:57.010 --> 00:11:58.350
Excuse me.

00:11:58.660 --> 00:12:01.360
I heard a bit of noise out here.

00:12:01.790 --> 00:12:03.610
Is something the matter?

00:12:03.610 --> 00:12:05.750
See? She came to us!

00:12:05.750 --> 00:12:09.100
Wait... are you the necromancer?

00:12:09.100 --> 00:12:11.230
O-Oh, I beg your pardon!

00:12:11.690 --> 00:12:14.700
I do indeed work as a necromancer.

00:12:14.700 --> 00:12:17.180
My name is Maria Deathflame.

00:12:17.180 --> 00:12:19.010
It's a pleasure to make your acquaintance.

00:12:19.220 --> 00:12:22.100
She's not exactly what I was expecting.

00:12:22.490 --> 00:12:24.690
She's totally ripping me off.

00:12:24.690 --> 00:12:27.220
Only on the "Deathflame" part.

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:29.560
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:30.800
I am Alvin.

00:12:30.800 --> 00:12:32.000
This is Carla.

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:34.220
Alvin-san and Carla-san.

00:12:34.610 --> 00:12:36.480
What lovely names!

00:12:36.720 --> 00:12:38.400
Y-You think so?

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:39.490
You're making me blush...

00:12:39.490 --> 00:12:42.740
I think Alvin is a wonderful name, too!

00:12:42.740 --> 00:12:44.090
It's better than you deserve!

00:12:44.090 --> 00:12:46.380
Oh, really? That pisses me off.

00:12:46.840 --> 00:12:49.100
What brings you two here?

00:12:49.100 --> 00:12:55.120
This is a forgotten graveyard, so I 
doubt you're here to see a grave...

00:12:55.390 --> 00:12:56.870
We are here to see a grave, actually.

00:12:57.520 --> 00:12:58.730
Yours!

00:12:58.730 --> 00:13:00.370
Just a moment, please!

00:13:00.790 --> 00:13:02.520
Why are you threatening violence?

00:13:02.520 --> 00:13:03.760
Are you trying to start a war?

00:13:04.030 --> 00:13:07.120
Zobita-san asked us to 
get revenge, remember?

00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:09.540
That's just him being petty!

00:13:09.540 --> 00:13:13.400
Besides, we're currently trying 
to convince him to reconsider!

00:13:13.960 --> 00:13:16.770
Wait! The warrior is that weak?

00:13:16.970 --> 00:13:20.770
You'd have a better chance 
in there than Alvin.

00:13:21.150 --> 00:13:23.870
So you should really just ditch 
this whole revenge idea.

00:13:23.870 --> 00:13:25.140
Fair enough.

00:13:25.620 --> 00:13:29.820
But a necromancer uses the dead! 
It's blasphemy!

00:13:29.820 --> 00:13:31.290
We can't just leave her at large!

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:34.420
I don't want to hear that from someone who 
blasphemes both the living and the dead.

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:37.110
I know she looks beautiful,

00:13:37.110 --> 00:13:39.370
but she's evil inside!

00:13:39.370 --> 00:13:41.520
What's that supposed to be, 
your new introduction?

00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:43.770
L-Look!

00:13:43.770 --> 00:13:45.940
And keep your voice down already!

00:13:46.170 --> 00:13:48.970
She's controlling all of those zombies!

00:13:49.370 --> 00:13:51.550
Maria-sama, hello!

00:13:51.550 --> 00:13:52.770
Hello!

00:13:52.770 --> 00:13:54.240
It's Maria-sama!

00:13:54.240 --> 00:13:56.350
Dance for us again, won't you?

00:13:56.580 --> 00:13:59.010
It looks more like they 
just really like her.

00:14:00.210 --> 00:14:03.180
I think she has blackmail material on them!

00:14:03.180 --> 00:14:05.780
Why would she bother?

00:14:06.370 --> 00:14:07.750
It's what I'd do.

00:14:07.750 --> 00:14:08.930
Maybe you should think about that!

00:14:08.930 --> 00:14:09.700
Hey!

00:14:09.980 --> 00:14:13.580
Are you guys badmouthing Maria-sama?

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:15.090
No, I...

00:14:15.090 --> 00:14:16.180
What's that?!

00:14:16.180 --> 00:14:19.400
Hey, she's the one who was 
chasing us around earlier!

00:14:19.400 --> 00:14:21.240
And she's a healer, isn't she?!

00:14:21.240 --> 00:14:22.390
The enemy of undead everywhere!

00:14:22.390 --> 00:14:25.590
You're here to hurt Maria-sama, aren't you?!

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:26.890
Hold on a minute.

00:14:26.890 --> 00:14:28.220
We can talk this out.

00:14:28.220 --> 00:14:29.460
That's right!

00:14:29.460 --> 00:14:30.740
With our fists!

00:14:31.950 --> 00:14:33.810
Just shut up already!

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:34.560
Maria♥

00:14:35.580 --> 00:14:37.340
You've shown your true face!

00:14:37.340 --> 00:14:38.880
Malevolent healer!

00:14:38.880 --> 00:14:41.070
We won't let you lay one hand on Maria-sama!

00:14:41.460 --> 00:14:43.570
No fighting, everyone!

00:14:43.850 --> 00:14:46.730
And remember, Carla is a holy woman!

00:14:46.730 --> 00:14:48.770
There's no way you can beat her!

00:14:48.770 --> 00:14:50.900
Even if it's a bad match-up for us,

00:14:50.900 --> 00:14:53.080
we will protect Maria-sama!

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:55.610
Get to safety while you can, Maria-sama!

00:14:55.610 --> 00:14:56.940
Bring it on!

00:14:56.940 --> 00:14:59.640
They're totally making us the villains here.

00:14:59.640 --> 00:15:02.330
They're like knights 
protecting their princess.

00:15:02.640 --> 00:15:04.360
We won't run this time!

00:15:04.360 --> 00:15:05.890
You won't beat us!

00:15:07.230 --> 00:15:10.290
Fighting to protect someone 
important to you...

00:15:10.660 --> 00:15:12.080
It's pretty cool.

00:15:12.350 --> 00:15:13.980
It is cool.

00:15:14.200 --> 00:15:15.450
Alvin-san.

00:15:15.450 --> 00:15:17.860
You have someone you could protect, too.

00:15:17.860 --> 00:15:19.620
Right, got it covered.

00:15:22.030 --> 00:15:23.970
So...?

00:15:23.970 --> 00:15:25.720
Shut up!

00:15:25.720 --> 00:15:29.370
Fine, I'll play along.

00:15:30.530 --> 00:15:33.040
I'm technically a frontline fighter, too!

00:15:33.040 --> 00:15:35.670
I won't let you harm Carla!

00:15:36.280 --> 00:15:37.620
Is that what you wanted?

00:15:37.970 --> 00:15:39.400
Alvin-san!

00:15:41.090 --> 00:15:42.890
I don't think you can win, though.

00:15:43.670 --> 00:15:45.030
Is this a joke?

00:15:47.740 --> 00:15:48.630
Okay!

00:15:52.730 --> 00:15:54.260
Is he trying to get himself killed?

00:15:59.630 --> 00:16:01.150
Now, bring it!

00:16:02.180 --> 00:16:04.730
Traitor! How dare you?!

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:07.810
Shut up! Stupid, stupid, stupid!

00:16:21.430 --> 00:16:23.820
Damn it! Let me out!

00:16:25.190 --> 00:16:26.490
Goodness me.

00:16:26.490 --> 00:16:28.730
Struggling won't get you anywhere.

00:16:28.730 --> 00:16:30.720
Conserve your strength.

00:16:31.100 --> 00:16:36.310
It's your own fault for 
betraying me back there.

00:16:36.670 --> 00:16:38.190
And, speaking of which...

00:16:38.580 --> 00:16:41.420
Why am I the only one in here?!

00:16:41.420 --> 00:16:43.930
Because I'm the one who arrested you.

00:16:44.290 --> 00:16:47.490
Why would the person doing the 
arresting up in the jail?

00:16:47.920 --> 00:16:49.530
Uncle! Uncle!

00:16:49.530 --> 00:16:51.560
I've captured the traitor!

00:16:51.560 --> 00:16:52.690
Throw him in jail!

00:16:52.690 --> 00:16:55.570
But thanks to you, we avoided a fight,

00:16:55.570 --> 00:16:57.570
and nobody got hurt!

00:16:57.570 --> 00:17:00.660
Except for my pride, which is in tatters.

00:17:00.930 --> 00:17:02.110
Oh, goodness!

00:17:02.110 --> 00:17:03.900
Maybe you'd be better off without it?

00:17:03.900 --> 00:17:04.800
Hey!

00:17:05.020 --> 00:17:10.170
At any rate, the zombies are currently 
discussing what to do with you.

00:17:10.170 --> 00:17:13.060
Once they realize you're worthless, 
they'll release you.

00:17:13.060 --> 00:17:14.430
Phrasing, please!

00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:18.200
Maria-san?

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:21.610
I'm sorry, you two.

00:17:21.610 --> 00:17:23.380
I didn't mean for this to happen.

00:17:23.380 --> 00:17:26.120
Really, there's no need 
for you to apologize!

00:17:26.120 --> 00:17:27.350
That's right.

00:17:27.350 --> 00:17:30.220
Just be more careful in 
the future, all right?

00:17:30.220 --> 00:17:32.100
You should be careful <i>all</i> the time!

00:17:32.100 --> 00:17:33.660
I'm sorry.

00:17:33.660 --> 00:17:35.460
But I...

00:17:35.810 --> 00:17:38.210
They had a discussion earlier, 
and they're considering...

00:17:38.730 --> 00:17:43.370
"That warrior... maybe we should 
turn him into a zombie."

00:17:44.570 --> 00:17:47.970
Hang on! Are you saying 
they're going to kill me?

00:17:47.970 --> 00:17:50.770
But he's already in jail! That's dead 
as far as society is concerned!

00:17:50.770 --> 00:17:51.980
I'm not dead!

00:17:51.980 --> 00:17:53.750
And <i>you're</i> the one who threw me in here!

00:17:53.990 --> 00:17:59.270
They all appear to want to 
make new zombies for my sake.

00:17:59.270 --> 00:18:02.630
But I don't think it's right to make 
someone a zombie without their consent.

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:05.230
So I brought the key to the cell.

00:18:05.230 --> 00:18:06.780
I want you to escape!

00:18:06.780 --> 00:18:08.150
You're sure?

00:18:08.380 --> 00:18:11.840
I haven't told the zombies.

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:14.160
This will be our little secret.

00:18:14.460 --> 00:18:16.040
What an angel!

00:18:16.040 --> 00:18:17.180
You called?

00:18:17.180 --> 00:18:18.620
Not you!

00:18:18.620 --> 00:18:20.580
Wait just a minute.

00:18:20.580 --> 00:18:24.230
As Alvin-san's companion, 
it is <i>my</i> duty to save him.

00:18:24.230 --> 00:18:27.000
You're the reason I'm in here!

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:29.290
And you don't even have the key!

00:18:29.290 --> 00:18:31.000
I do have an unlock spell!

00:18:32.730 --> 00:18:34.750
It works by blowing up the lock!

00:18:34.750 --> 00:18:36.510
What are you, a saboteur?!

00:18:36.860 --> 00:18:38.180
This is a good opportunity.

00:18:38.180 --> 00:18:42.130
Let's compete to see who 
can save Alvin-san first!

00:18:42.350 --> 00:18:44.420
Against a necromancer of darkness,

00:18:44.420 --> 00:18:47.900
a healer of light could not possibly lose!

00:18:47.900 --> 00:18:50.270
You got the darkness and light backwards.

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:54.020
But all Maria-san has to do 
is unlock the door, so...

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:55.530
Except...

00:18:55.850 --> 00:18:58.570
I'm not sure which key it is now!

00:18:58.570 --> 00:18:59.460
So many!

00:18:59.460 --> 00:19:00.780
What will I do?!

00:19:00.780 --> 00:19:02.230
N-No problem!

00:19:02.230 --> 00:19:04.150
Just remain calm and try them one at a time!

00:19:04.150 --> 00:19:05.330
That's right.

00:19:05.330 --> 00:19:07.640
Just stay calm and go slow.

00:19:07.640 --> 00:19:11.130
I'll enjoy my final conversation 
with Alvin-san the same way.

00:19:11.130 --> 00:19:13.200
This was a competition 
to <i>save<i>

00:19:13.740 --> 00:19:15.430
Let me recite my chant.</i></i>

00:19:15.790 --> 00:19:18.170
Let me see... Let me see...

00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:21.420
This one doesn't fit, either...

00:19:22.510 --> 00:19:23.460
You're doing fine.

00:19:23.460 --> 00:19:24.910
Just try the next key!

00:19:26.250 --> 00:19:28.070
Ten...

00:19:29.120 --> 00:19:31.240
Nine...

00:19:32.050 --> 00:19:33.020
Eh?

00:19:32.430 --> 00:19:34.250
Eight...

00:19:33.020 --> 00:19:35.550
Maria-san, I think you 
tried that one already!

00:19:35.770 --> 00:19:37.300
Seven...

00:19:35.990 --> 00:19:38.080
What? What?

00:19:38.080 --> 00:19:41.840
Which is it? Which is it?!

00:19:38.700 --> 00:19:40.300
Four...

00:19:39.840 --> 00:19:41.280
Why did you skip a number?!

00:19:41.280 --> 00:19:42.570
Stop the countdown!

00:19:42.800 --> 00:19:44.570
Three...

00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:47.150
Th-The pressure is...

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:47.570
Two...

00:19:48.830 --> 00:19:50.370
Are you all right?

00:19:48.830 --> 00:19:50.630
One...

00:19:50.680 --> 00:19:51.830
I'm sorry.

00:19:51.830 --> 00:19:53.150
I'm sorry!

00:19:53.760 --> 00:19:54.830
I'm sorry...

00:19:55.090 --> 00:19:56.270
Let me see...

00:19:56.270 --> 00:19:57.330
I'm sorry.

00:19:59.200 --> 00:20:00.720
Um... Um...

00:20:01.180 --> 00:20:03.160
I can't watch this.

00:20:03.970 --> 00:20:05.870
Carla-san, what about your chant?

00:20:05.870 --> 00:20:07.650
Never mind that.

00:20:07.650 --> 00:20:12.180
Let's start by eliminating the keys 
that obviously won't fit the hole.

00:20:12.180 --> 00:20:13.590
R-Right.

00:20:13.970 --> 00:20:15.320
Is this even a key?

00:20:15.810 --> 00:20:19.260
You really should put 
labels on these things.

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:21.990
Or maybe split them up based on purpose.

00:20:22.250 --> 00:20:23.470
Yes, you're right.

00:20:23.470 --> 00:20:25.110
I'll start doing that from now on.

00:20:25.310 --> 00:20:27.100
Watching you has made me think.

00:20:27.100 --> 00:20:29.990
You're actually rather hopeless, aren't you?

00:20:32.420 --> 00:20:34.340
What's so funny?

00:20:34.740 --> 00:20:36.570
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:41.940
I was thinking, 
you're kinder than you seemed.

00:20:54.930 --> 00:20:57.250
Thank you.

00:21:06.010 --> 00:21:07.570
Hang on a minute.

00:21:07.810 --> 00:21:09.750
Carla, kind?

00:21:10.500 --> 00:21:12.450
Yeah, right. Don't make me laugh!

00:21:12.450 --> 00:21:15.780
Kind? More like bizarre!

00:21:25.510 --> 00:21:27.810
Uh, what just happened?

00:21:28.160 --> 00:21:30.260
Stay over tonight, would you?

00:21:30.260 --> 00:21:31.920
If it comes with food, sure.

00:21:34.730 --> 00:21:36.270
H-Hang on, you two!

00:21:36.840 --> 00:21:38.940
You haven't unlocked the door yet!

00:21:39.230 --> 00:21:40.260
Why?!

00:21:40.990 --> 00:21:42.680
Hey!

00:21:43.650 --> 00:21:45.280
Hey!

00:21:45.950 --> 00:21:47.520
Hey...

00:21:47.520 --> 00:21:48.740
Unlock the—

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:26.550 --> 00:23:29.540
Are you sure you want me doing the preview?

00:23:29.540 --> 00:23:33.020
As you know, I work as a necromancer,

00:23:33.020 --> 00:23:34.470
and my name is Maria Deathflame.

00:23:34.700 --> 00:23:36.330
I'll be introducing the next episode now.

00:23:36.330 --> 00:23:37.390
I hope you please watch it!

00:23:37.010 --> 00:23:39.970
<b>See you then!</b>

00:23:37.010 --> 00:23:40.090
<b>"Thanks to Altargaia (reminder: this is the mushroom's name),
Alvin gets out of the cell safe and sound but now that Carla and
Maria are unexpectedly getting along they continue leading him
around by the nose and it happens that Maria has a sweet little
sister named Ellie and while avoiding spoilers regarding
what trouble Ellie's gotten into it does concern Maria's status
as a necromancer but I hope you won't get your hopes up for
another cute female character to appear but in exchange
Carla will attempt an unusual cosplay so that's the part you can
look forward to and that's the deal with episode 8."</b>

00:23:37.390 --> 00:23:40.060
Now! Next week's title is—
